    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>A corrupt Tammany Hall-era financier who bought his way into the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.6868ee8c357f4b73]{Sabbat} via a @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.OpCOs3PLjmtl0QVu]{Ventrue} sire, Douglas &ldquo;Boss&rdquo; Callihan grew disillusioned with the sect's lack of refinement and defected to the nascent anarch movement, rising to become one of New York's most prominent anarch bosses. He deliberately kept his anarchs out of the Battle of New York hoping to seize the spoils once the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.6868ee8c357f4b73]{Sabbat} and @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.fc464242d84d4e34]{Camarilla} exhausted each other, but the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.fc464242d84d4e34]{Camarilla}'s swift victory left the anarchs relegated to Staten Island. In its aftermath, Callihan hired an @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.WaQFCEXFzv8YeAgX]{Assamite} to assassinate ascending Prince Calebros and destabilize rival domains for an anarch land-grab; the harpy Hellene Panhard uncovered the plot, intercepted the assassin, and extracted a blood bond from Callihan in exchange for her silence. He now waits, chafing, for the political situation to loosen enough to move against the Camarilla again.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>The anarch cause is secondary to your own advancement; you tell the anarchs what they want to hear in exchange for their loyalty as a personal army, and you would drop the movement in a heartbeat for a better opportunity &mdash; though you keep that fact carefully hidden.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Thomas Albee. Secretly Blood Bound to the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.fc464242d84d4e34]{Camarilla} harpy Hellene Panhard after she uncovered his plot to have Prince Calebros assassinated. Ratings above 5 from the original stat block have been capped to fit this system's 1-5 scale.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
